        "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n  <title>RFC 9101 - OAuth JAR</title>\n  <script src=\"https://polyfill.io/v3/polyfill.min.js?features=es6\"></script>\n  <script id=\"MathJax-script\" async src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-mml-chtml.js\"></script>\n  <style>\n    * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n    html, body {\n      margin: 0;\n      padding: 0;\n      background: #ffffff;\n      color: #252525;\n    }\n    body {\n      font-family: \"Times New Roman\", Times, serif;\n    }\n    .page {\n      position: relative;\n      width: 1653px;\n      min-height: 2325px;\n      margin: 0 auto;\n      background: #fff;\n      overflow: hidden;\n    }\n    .top-header {\n      position: absolute;\n      top: 99px;\n      left: 155px;\n      width: 1342px;\n      height: 59px;\n      border-bottom: 2px solid #d2d2d2;\n      font-size: 27px;\n      line-height: 42px;\n    }\n    .top-header .left { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; }\n    .top-header .center { position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; top: 0; text-align: center; }\n    .top-header .right { position: absolute; right: 0; top: 0; }\n\n    main {\n      position: absolute;\n      left: 183px;\n      top: 257px;\n      width: 1287px;\n      font-size: 30px;\n      line-height: 1.25;\n    }\n    h1 {\n      margin: 0 0 21px 0;\n      font-size: 43px;\n      line-height: 1.18;\n      font-weight: bold;\n    }\n    p {\n      margin: 0 0 28px 0;\n    }\n    a {\n      color: #1717b9;\n      text-decoration: none;\n    }\n    code {\n      font-family: \"Courier New\", Courier, monospace;\n      font-size: .88em;\n      background: #f8f8f8;\n      padding: 0 2px;\n    }\n    .example {\n      width: 1287px;\n      height: 145px;\n      margin: 27px 0 28px 0;\n      padding: 26px 89px;\n      border: 2px solid #eeeeee;\n      background: #fafafa;\n      font-family: \"Courier New\", Courier, monospace;\n      font-size: 27px;\n      line-height: 1.12;\n      white-space: pre;\n    }\n    .after-example {\n      margin-bottom: 29px;\n    }\n    .shortcomings {\n      margin-top: 54px;\n      margin-bottom: 29px;\n      width: 1250px;\n    }\n    .shortcomings .item,\n    .reasons .item {\n      display: grid;\n      grid-template-columns: 83px 1fr;\n      column-gap: 0;\n      margin: 6px 0;\n    }\n    .shortcomings .label,\n    .reasons .label {\n      white-space: nowrap;\n    }\n    .shortcomings .text {\n      padding-left: 0;\n    }\n    .spaced {\n      margin-top: 28px;\n      margin-bottom: 28px;\n    }\n    .reasons-intro {\n      margin-top: 29px;\n      margin-bottom: 56px;\n    }\n    .reasons {\n      width: 1260px;\n    }\n    .reasons .item {\n      margin: 7px 0;\n    }\n    .reasons .label {\n      width: 83px;\n    }\n    .footer {\n      position: absolute;\n      left: 155px;\n      top: 1981px;\n      width: 1342px;\n      height: 80px;\n      padding-top: 24px;\n      border-top: 2px solid #d2d2d2;\n      font-size: 27px;\n      line-height: 35px;\n    }\n    .footer .left { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 24px; }\n    .footer .center { position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; top: 24px; text-align: center; }\n    .footer .right { position: absolute; right: 0; top: 24px; }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <div class=\"page\">\n    <header class=\"top-header\">\n      <span class=\"left\">RFC 9101</span>\n      <span class=\"center\">OAuth JAR</span>\n      <span class=\"right\">August 2021</span>\n    </header>\n\n    <main>\n      <h1>1.&nbsp;&nbsp; Introduction</h1>\n\n      <p>The authorization request in <a href=\"#\">OAuth 2.0</a> [<a href=\"#\">RFC6749</a>] utilizes query parameter serialization and is<br>typically sent through user agents such as web browsers.</p>\n\n      <p>For example, the parameters <code>response_type</code>, <code>client_id</code>, <code>state</code>, and <code>redirect_uri</code> are encoded<br>in the URI of the request:</p>\n\n      <div class=\"example\">GET /authorize?response_type=code&amp;client_id=s6BhdRkqt3&amp;state=xyz\n&amp;redirect_uri=https%3A%2F%2Fclient%2Eexample%2Ecom%2Fcb HTTP/1.1\nHost: server.example.com</div>\n\n      <p class=\"after-example\">While it is easy to implement, the encoding in the URI does not allow application-layer security to<br>be used to provide confidentiality and integrity protection. While TLS is used to offer<br>communication security between the client and the user agent as well as the user agent and the<br>authorization server, TLS sessions are terminated in the user agent. In addition, TLS sessions<br>may be terminated prematurely at some middlebox (such as a load balancer).</p>\n\n      <p>As a result, the authorization request of [<a href=\"#\">RFC6749</a>] has shortcomings in that:</p>\n\n      <div class=\"shortcomings\">\n        <div class=\"item\">\n          <div class=\"label\">(a)</div>\n          <div class=\"text\">the communication through the user agents is not integrity protected, and thus, the<br>parameters can be tainted (integrity protection failure);</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"item\">\n          <div class=\"label\">(b)</div>\n          <div class=\"text\">the source of the communication is not authenticated (source authentication failure);</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"item\">\n          <div class=\"label\">(c)</div>\n          <div class=\"text\">the communication through the user agents can be monitored (containment/<br>confidentiality failure).</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <p class=\"spaced\">Due to these inherent weaknesses, several attacks against the protocol, such as redirection URI<br>rewriting, have been identified.</p>\n\n      <p class=\"spaced\">The use of application-layer security mitigates these issues.</p>\n\n      <p class=\"spaced\">The use of application-layer security allows requests to be prepared by a trusted third party so<br>that a client application cannot request more permissions than previously agreed upon.</p>\n\n      <p class=\"spaced\">Furthermore, passing the request by reference allows the reduction of over-the-wire overhead.</p>\n\n      <p class=\"reasons-intro\">The <a href=\"#\">JWT</a> [<a href=\"#\">RFC7519</a>] encoding has been chosen because of:</p>\n\n      <div class=\"reasons\">\n        <div class=\"item\">\n          <div class=\"label\">(1)</div>\n          <div>its close relationship with JSON, which is used as OAuth's response format</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"item\">\n          <div class=\"label\">(2)</div>\n          <div>its developer friendliness due to its textual nature</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"item\">\n          <div class=\"label\">(3)</div>\n          <div>its relative compactness compared to XML</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"item\">\n          <div class=\"label\">(4)</div>\n          <div>its development status as a Proposed Standard, along with the associated signing and<br>encryption methods [<a href=\"#\">RFC7515</a>] [<a href=\"#\">RFC7516</a>]</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </main>\n\n    <footer class=\"footer\">\n      <span class=\"left\">Sakimura, et al.</span>\n      <span class=\"center\">Standards Track</span>\n      <span class=\"right\">Page 4</span>\n    </footer>\n  </div>\n</body>\n</html>"
